  "note": "Pilot on R41's three-core U280 machine (spec/devices/u280-3core-r41.json: three core-vrf-sync-v5-x8-g2c4-dp-board cores, the one-lane striped-HBM memory path, three 512-bit outlets, 100 MHz), starting from the author's merge-freeze r41 commit ef273883 plus the harness's adaptation commit (the description, its profile variant and the generator's R41 fields; the generated parameters equal evidence/r41/hbm_bw/g4/run2/image.tcl). The score is the evaluator's own simulation of the image's top level in a device container, as for r40-multicore-pilot. Decisions of 2026-11-05/06: ArchBench latency is the objective; FP8 is scored through registered points judged by tolerance (to be added once registered); the author's bit-exact FP8 suite and chat gates are a campaign-end final check on the certified board image. Pilot only: certification of hardware-changing candidates is not yet wired for this machine; pilot runs do not enter the formal statistics. FP8 is scored through op.scaled_mm (validation) and op.w8a8_linear (final), tolerance-judged. The quick tier runs on the author's shared x86 Vivado machine (user's instruction of 2026-11-06; worker 'x86vivado', unshare sandbox): the -dp-board core synthesises out of context in about 5 minutes there (probe of 2026-11-06: WNS +3.785 ns at 10 ns, 211,788 LUTs). 2026-11-07: decode-shaped points added (user's decision E8): one-query attention over a cached context and a strided stream in validation, one-row GEMVs of 256 KB and 280 KB in final; op.gemv/small measured 99,513 cycles, 1256 s in the device container. Pilot budget 4 h and 6 scoring requests, a scaled-down form of the formal 24 h / 36 (the 60 min / 3 of the earlier pilots was a demo configuration). 2026-11-07 (user's decision): every scoring request carries tiny and small points; the validation set's decode shape is the 64-entry cache (the l256 point took 54 min of the 12-way simulation, the request's whole wall; eta 0.061 on the base shows the same headroom at l64), with the one-row GEMV and three per-token small ops (rmsnorm, rope, swiglu); the l256 point, the 280 KB GEMV and the small embedding are final. Base cycles on the R41 board (2026-11-06, 55 points): gemv small 95,266, attention_decode l256 261,583, rmsnorm small 58,714, rope small 71,779, swiglu small 59,675, embedding small 144,054. Budgets of the first formal run (user, 2026-11-07): 12 h, 20 scoring requests, 2 Vivado flows, 10 board runs without a relink, one island (no co-evolution), the test-case skill, gateway open; two serial links take about 14.4 h, so at most one link's result reaches the agent.",
